  "description": "The Hackathon at Vishnu Institute of Technology, Bhimavaram (VITB) is a platform that is created to foster innovation, creativity, and problem-solving among students. It provides a unique opportunity for participants to work collaboratively in teams and develop solutions to real-world challenges. This event is not just a competition, but also a learning experience where students can enhance their technical skills, improve teamwork, and gain valuable exposure to innovation-driven problem-solving. Eligibility Criteria The hackathon is open for the Under Graduate all over India, as this event is meant to encourage internal talent and collaboration. All years B. Tech students from all engineering branches (AI&DS, CSE, IT, ECE, EEE, Mechanical, Civil, AI &ML, etc.) are eligible. This ensures fair competition among students with similar levels of exposure and knowledge. Inter-college teams are allowed.",
